# Quizly frontend environment
# Next.js loads frontend/.env.local. This file is a reference/template.
# Copy it to .env.local only once; after that, switch modes by commenting
# or uncommenting the blocks below instead of copying files repeatedly.
# All frontend REST calls use the same-origin /backend proxy in LAN and ONLINE
# modes. NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL selects the upstream; do not configure a browser-side
# REST URL separately for either mode.
#
# ========================== ONLINE MODE ==========================
# Active by default: local frontend uses the hosted Spring Boot backend.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=ONLINE
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://quiz-app-s033.onrender.com
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
# AI proctoring service for local development (Python service on port 8000).
# Local development defaults. Set these to the deployed AI service in production.
# Use HTTPS for the HTTP URL and WSS for the WebSocket URL when the frontend uses HTTPS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL=http://localhost:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000
# Production deployments must set the deployed HTTPS/WSS AI service URLs in the hosting environment.
# Do not rely on a temporary ngrok tunnel as a permanent production endpoint.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL=https://your-deployed-ai-service.example
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL=wss://your-deployed-ai-service.example
#
# ============================ LAN MODE ============================
# To use the backend on your Wi-Fi/LAN:
# 1. Comment the three active ONLINE lines above.
# 2. Uncomment these three LAN lines.
# 3. Replace both IP addresses if your Wi-Fi assigns different addresses.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=LAN
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.29.139.67:8080
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=10.210.254.230:3000
#
# ========================== IMPORTANT ============================
# - Keep exactly ONE NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE and ONE NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL active.
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the Spring Boot backend's origin/address.
#   Google sign-in navigates directly to this origin at /oauth2/authorization/google
#   so the Spring Security OAuth session/state stays on the backend host.
#   Do NOT set it to the frontend origin (for example localhost:3000) or to
#   the frontend's /backend proxy route. Use the backend origin, such as
#   http://localhost:8080 locally or the deployed Spring Boot API origin online.
# - ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS is a comma-separated list of host:port values for
#   Next.js development origins (for example, localhost:3000). Do not include
#   http:// or https://, and do not use the backend address unless that is also
#   the address used to open Next.js. Do not use 0.0.0.0; it is only a bind address.
# - For a backend running on this same computer, use:
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
#     ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
# - After changing .env.local, stop and restart the Next.js server.
#   For a production build, rebuild after changing NEXT_PUBLIC_* values.
